Halftone print effect (the `halftone` function, `HALFTONE_SCREENS` and `_simplex2` in nodes/main.py)
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
This part is a NumPy port of glsl-halftone (index.glsl, version 1.0.4):
  https://github.com/glslify/glsl-halftone
glsl-halftone adapts Stefan Gustavson's WebGL halftone shader (public domain) and uses
glsl-aastep (https://github.com/glslify/glsl-aastep, MIT, Copyright (c) 2015 stackgl) and the
2D simplex noise from glsl-noise / Ashima Arts webgl-noise (https://github.com/hughsk/glsl-noise,
https://github.com/ashima/webgl-noise, MIT).
Changes from the original: GLSL rewritten in NumPy for still images; dot radius multiplied by
sqrt(4/pi) ~ 1.128 so the dot area equals the ink amount; dot frequency set by cell
count along the long side (150, 105, 70 for low, medium, high); the anti-aliasing width uses the
analytic pixel step of the grid distance plus neighbor-pixel differences of ink and noise; the
noise lattice hash is computed with integers.

